>based upon what I've seen thus far, that these Boxer fans in the 8/e
>use sleeve bearings instead of ball bearings?  If so, should I use a

Quite likely. Often (but by no means always) low voltage fans seem to use 
ball bearings and higher voltage fans sleeve bearings. I can think of no 
good reason for this, and IIRC, I've actually seen all 4 combinations in 
the catalogues.

>different type of lubricant on them?

Yes. Ball bearings need grease, while sleeve bearings need a light machine
oil. In a lot of cases, the sleeve bearings will soak up oil to some extent,
and leaving them in a bath of oil overnight is a good idea.

>Here's what I've done so far to remove the fan blade and commutator
                                                           ^^^^^
You mean rotor here, unless it's a very odd fan. I've never seen a brush and
commutator motor used in a muffin fan.

