In article <1996Apr27.144407.538@macro.demon.co.uk>, Neill Clift
<neill@macro.demon.co.uk> writes
>I want to hook up a couple of RA72s to a 3900. I have a kda50 that is two cards
>on the qbus connected by a couple of ribbon cables. From one card comes some
>thick black leads that plug into one of two ports in the back of the RA72. If I
>just plug one leed into any of the two ports and plug in the power surply the
>dive shows up to a console 'show dev' command and I can mount the device under
>VMS. If I connected both ports up on one disk or one port from each of two
>different disks the device type shows up as @0 so its obviosly not happy. I
>notice that there is 3 dip switches on the RA72 but changing these with a
>single device did not change the device number. Can anyone enlighten me on what
>does what on this system? I would like to put two RA72s in if possible. Are
>these RA72s dual ported?
>
>Thanks.
>                                 Neill.

The three switches are for:

        Switch          Use
        ======          ===
        1               Down for RA72 (Up for RA71)
        2               Unit select
        3               Unit select

The four drives on the KDA50 must have a different address, therefore 
the two RA72's must have switches 2 & 3 in different positions.

Hope this helps.



-- 
Graham Godfrey



