X-Deja-AN: 151445807
distribution: world
references: <4l5ot6$o1t@news.aero.org>
organization: Digital Equipment Corp
reply-to: hoffman@xdelta.enet.dec.com (Stephen Hoffman)
newsgroups: comp.os.vms,vmsnet.alpha,comp.sys.dec


In article <4l5ot6$o1t@news.aero.org>, johnson@halley.aero.org ("Wowbagger the Infinitely Prolonged") writes:

:Can a RRD40 CD-ROM drive be attached to a DEC 3000/400 running VMS?  I 
:vaguely remember there is some sort of problem with doing that.

   Yaacov's (fenster@star.enet.dec.com) comments to the contrary, I would
   not recommend using the RRD40 on Alpha systems, and I would particularly
   not recommend it in OpenVMS Alpha SCSI cluster configurations.  (The
   RRD42, RRD43, and RRD44 CD-ROM drives are far better choices for use
   on OpenVMS Alpha systems.)

   Check the Software Product Description (SPD) for information on device
   support -- per the V7.0 SPD, the RRD40 CD-ROM drive is not supported on
   OpenVMS Alpha systems.  (It is supported on various OpenVMS VAX platforms.)

  ------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
   Stephen Hoffman      OpenVMS Engineering      hoffman@xdelta.enet.dec.com
