In article <317f3e08.410344@10.10.1.225>, netboy@kbsi.com (Sheldon) writes:
|>I have a Digital Prioris Server with a DEC TLZ07 DAT drive running
|>Arcserve for Netware.  Arcserve says that compression is on, but I am
|>now getting full tape errors, and I have no where near 8 gig of disk
|>space on the server, but I have more than 4 gigs.
|>
|>I have a RAID controller and an Adaptec 2940 SCSI-II PCI controller.
|>I believe that DAT drive is running off the Adaptec.  I am using the
|>APSI50 driver in Arcserve.  Could this be the problem?
|>
|>Anyone else have this problem?  Does the TLZ07 have a jumper on it
|>that I need to check or is it all software?
|>
|>Thanks for any info
|>
|>Sheldon
|>

There is a switch on the TLZ07 that needs to be set to enable compression.

We found three switch packs on ours, none of them being exactly where
the docs said (surprise!).  We have a TLZ07-DA, it's the tabletop version.

On ours, while in the enclosure, there are four switches in a panel on the 
back of the enclosure. Three of them are used to set the SCSI address. If we
open up the enclosure, there is a set of switches on the back of the tape drive 
(where the SCSI cabling connects to those switches on the enclosure). There are
eight switches there. (A flashlight and a magnifying glass can be helpful here,
by the way). Number 6 is the compression switch. Up is off, down is on.
They are numbered right to left. This needs to be turned OFF to enable
compaction. 

