>Can anybody tell me if I can yse Digital monitor model VR160-DA with my 
>PC and what I would need to do so? Please help.
>                                      Jack Kostanski

Not really easy - this screen uses sync on green which no standard pc
cards support. Also, it is fixed frequency which means that even if
you did get it to work, it would only run graphics eg windows at
1024/768. Dos text screen would be just a blur.

There is one way you might do it... try http://www.photonweb.com.
This outfit produce cards to allow just this type of screen to 
be used on PC - havn't tried myself but I hear good reports...

Good luck 

Mike




