In article <4lo4s3$cnc_001@news.fast.net>, kshuff@fast.net (kshuff) writes:
>
>... two hard drives (RZ23L and RZ24). 
>but I have no idea whats on the drives, I assume a version of Ultrix.

If ULTRIX is installed on either drive it will be the RZ24, which
is (barely) supported as a system disk.  You can't fit much of a
system on one, but I guess a minimal installation will fit on one.
That will allowing move stuff to the other disk to free up space
on the first.

>What do 
>I need to set the bootpath and bootmode to get this thing to boot?

The bootpath syntax is:

dev(controller,target,partition)filename

Where the components are:

dev:

   rz - SCSI disk
   tz - SCSI tape
   mop - Maintenance Operations Protocol network boot
	 (Note: mop doesn't use any of the other parameters,
	  so the bootpath for network boot is "mop()")

controller: Always 0.

target: SCSI target ID of the device.

partition: Partition index of disk; a = 0, b = 1, c = 2, etc.

filename: Filename of file to boot.  Typically this is /vmunix
or /genvmunix.

The choices for bootmode are:

* - Default
a - Autoboot using bootpath
d - Reset the workstation without running selftests.
r - Try to restart (not that ULTRIX supported it...)

As I recollect "boot" uses bootmode to boot to single user, while
"auto" boots to multi-user.

>Is there 
>any way to access the disks from console mode to determine whats on them?

Not that I recall.  You need to boot a system.  If you have another ULTRIX
system setup for Remote Installation Services or a tape or CDROM and ULTRIX
distribution you can boot the standalone system and use that to check the
disks.

>How are the drives assigned and designated?

rz# where # is the SCSI target ID.  The DECstation 3100 only had a single
SCSI bus, so device numbering was very easy.

>And finally, if anyone would have a 
>manual for this beast, I sure would appreciate a copy.

The part numbers for hardware installation guide and operator's guide are:

EK-290AB-IN-002
EK-302AB-OG-002

