:is the only scale I'd accept!)

You are confusing boot duration with time-until-crash.

Sometimes I have to boot my SGI Indigo workstation ten times a day  --
but it hasn't *crashed* for 8 months (at which time a series of
closely-spaced power spikes caused it to mis-read memory.) Why reboot
it then? Because I swap perhipherals in and out and install new system
software, and generally use my system as a testbed for new hardware and
software. At such times, the faster it reboots, the faster I'm back in
operation.

