> We're considering the Alpha XL/266 now with eventual 
upgrade to the XL/366. I've been told the 366 will have 8 
memory slots which are filled in in pairs. Is this correct?

Yes, it has 8 memory slots, and no, the memory must be filled 
in sets of 4 SIMMs.

> Is the 266 memory compatible?

Yes.

> What does DEC do if your 266 has 3 simms?

You cannot have any working 266 or 366 with 3 SIMMs.
Either 2 or 4.
 
> How does the 366's 128bit memory path compare to the 266's 
64bit path?

It is a bit difficult to extract the effect of the wider
memory bus in these systems. What you could do is to
compare our late AlphaStation 250 4/266 with an XL 266.
The 250 has a 128-bit memory bus and XL 266 has a 64-bit
memory bus. The CPU is the same for these two systems.

Unfortunately I was unable to find a benchmark where these
two would be mentioned.

