A low-power mode is better for this.  On my notebook I leave it in sleep
mode when I'm not using it, and on my UNIX box at home I leave the computer 
on all the time and the monitor goes into power-saving mode in three stages
(first screen blanker, then light sleep, then deep sleep).  There's no need
to change the boot process.  In both cases it's usually weeks or months
for me between reboots.

