John Leonard wrote:
> 
> We're considering the Alpha XL/266 now with eventual upgrade to the
> XL/366. I've been told the 366 will have 8 memory slots which are filled
> in in pairs. Is this correct? Is the 266 memory compatible? What does DEC
> do if your 266 has 3 simms? How does the 366's 128bit memory path
> compare to the 266's 64bit path? Any definitive info on this would be
> greatly appreciated.
> 
> -John jleonard@titan.com


The Alpha XL/266 is upgradeable to the XL/366.  If you are buying the 
XL/266 new it will come with 36bit SIMMS (older units shipped with 33 bit 
SIMMS).  The 36 bit simms are used on the XL/366.  The upgrade to the 
XL/366 will come with a new CPU card and a new motherboard (due to the 
128 bit memory path.  Memory must be populated in 4's on the XL/366.

Jeff
