In article <317f3e08.410344@10.10.1.225>, netboy@kbsi.com (Sheldon) writes:
>I have a Digital Prioris Server with a DEC TLZ07 DAT drive running
>Arcserve for Netware.  Arcserve says that compression is on, but I am
>now getting full tape errors, and I have no where near 8 gig of disk
>space on the server, but I have more than 4 gigs.
>
>I have a RAID controller and an Adaptec 2940 SCSI-II PCI controller.
>I believe that DAT drive is running off the Adaptec.  I am using the
>APSI50 driver in Arcserve.  Could this be the problem?

What problem is that?  

You've indicated that you have a TLZ07 tape drive, and that you don't think
that you're getting 8GB of storage out of it.  But, you haven't indicated a
problem.

However, if your problem is that you're supposed to be getting 8GB/tape, then
there's several things you can check.

1) That 8GB/tape is assuming a compression ratio of 2:1.  What is your data? 
If you have 4GB of .ZIP files, then they'll take 4GB of tape, since .ZIP files
are already compressed.

2) Remember that backup programs put more than just your data on the tape. 
They include some control information, and some backup programs use redundancy 
to help make sure you can recover your data.  

3) That 8GB/tape is valid only if you use a 120m DDS-2 tape.  What kind of
tapes are you using?

