In article <4lu5ba$h9q@news.cic.net>, jhiggins@cedar.cic.net (John Higgins) writes:
> I received an R400X drive cabinet with 6 rf35/rz35 drives in it. I can 
> not get the unit to work using the SCSI connection (M7493-PA) when 
> pluged into my Adaptec 1542cf on my PC. The drives spin up in the unit 
> and are all green lights, however no devices are seen by the PC. Are 
> there any jumpers on the drive to change them from RF35 to RZ35? I 
> called Dec and the CSC told me just to plug into the SCSI and disconnect 
> the DSSI cables, and it should work. It didn't. Anybody got any ideas?

  The drive logic is *not* the same for RF35's and SCSI. If you have RF-
series DSSI disks, they won't be visible to any SCSI controllers.

  The later R400X expanders had both DSSI and SCSI bus connectors as well
as internal busing. I *think* the SCSI bus only shows up at the larger
slot on the top right hand side, which can be used for a SCSI tape drive.

