In article <4lmmg8$f67@Mars.mcs.com>, 
fluke@MCS.COM (Greg Linder) writes:

> I recently gathered together all the elements to make my 
> VAXStation II/GPX machine a usable system.   Unfortunately, there
> is a problem somewhere between the video card and the end
> of the cable.

> <snip>

> ...if someone can provide me with the pinouts of the
> two video output ports (The one in the middle of the rear side
> of the board, as well as the one directly in front of the
> Digital logo on the board) on the video card itself, then I can
> make a cable to go to a properly wired connector, and finally
> be successful in the way of having a functional VAXStation II
> machine.

First of all, there is only a single video output connector on the
VCB02 (M7169).   If you hold the board so that the fingers are down
and the components are towards you, you should see along the top:

    50-pin connector to M7168 memory board(s).

    3 LEDs (status indicators)

    20-pin connector for video/mouse/keyboard

    20-pin connector to the first M7168 memory board.
    This connector is just above the "digital" logo.

Below and slightly to the right of this connector is:

    20-pin connector to the second M7168 memory board.
    This connector is just below the "digital" logo.

As for the pinouts of the video/mouse/keyboard connector,
the attached text is a reply to a previous person who asked
these questions.   The quoted text near the end is from
his question.   If all this is not clear, e-mail me your
FAX number and I will FAX the diagrams to you.

Good luck with your system.

Alan

--  Alan E. Frisbie               Frisbie@Flying-Disk.Com
