>   I have a Microvax II and a 3200. My problem is that i have a third
>party vendor SCSI dirver board that is used to operate a 8mm Tape
>drive labeled as MUA0: .  I have tried with no success in installing a
>TK50 Tape drive and controller into my system. I have changed the
>vector address from 260 to the 2 other jumper settings that are
>recommened in my hardware book.  I Have pulled out the SCSI and it
>still does not  see the controller unless i use the default address of
>260. At the" >>>" prompt  I type " show dev" and only one TK50 comes
>up with both controllers are installed and that controller is the 8mm
>drive.  My manual states that it should come up with a driver label of
>MUB0:. Is it possible that i need to do a low level config? and if so
>how do i go about doing this.      I would be very Greatful for any
>help !     
>Troy Reitz     Email address Reitz@calweb.com
