distribution: world
references: <317B2F4A.3D08@regent.e-technik.tu-muenchen.de>
organization: Digital Equipment Corporation
reply-to: alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com (Alan Rollow - Dr. File System's Home for Wayward Inodes.)
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


In article <317B2F4A.3D08@regent.e-technik.tu-muenchen.de>, tobias Abthoff <toa@regent.e-technik.tu-muenchen.de> writes:

>does anybody know how to install an MO-Drive (DEC RWZ52) under 
>Digital Unix ??

Select a unique SCSI ID for the bus on which you want to install
the drive.  Shutdown the system and add the device to the bus.
At this point verify that the particualr console can see the
device.  Boot Digital UNIX.

Then go buy a product that will license use of the CLC Optical Driver
since that seems to be the only way to read/write SCSI "Optical" devices.
The CLC kits are on the considated distribution and will have a copy
of the SPD in the documentation directory for the kit (clc300 or clc220).
The SPD for the Optical driver should have a list of all the products
that license use of the driver.

Unfortunately, the SCSI CAM disk driver seems to be very particular
about what sort of device it will support; direct access.  So, if the
RWZ52 reports itself as "Optical", the CAM disk driver won't touch it.
>
