Subject: version 4.2 of Vis5D is now available
Date: 1996/04/18
Message-ID: <4l5ois$b6g@spool.cs.wisc.edu>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 148197524
organization: University of WI, Madison -- Computer Sciences Dept.
newsgroups: comp.sys.sgi.apps,comp.sys.hp.apps,comp.sys.dec,k12.ed.science


Version 4.2 of Vis5D is now available.  Vis5D provides highly
interactive visualization of simulations of the atmosphere and
oceans.  The major new features of version 4.2 are:

  An API (Application Programming Interface) between the Vis5D
    user interface and Vis5D graphics and data managament.  The
    API makes it easy for system developers to use Vis5D as a
    visualization subsystem of their own systems.  The API is
    used by the the Vis5D GUI (Graphical User Interface), by the
    Vis5D scripting language (described below), and by the NASA
    GSFC Interactive Image SpreadSheet,

  A scripting language based on Tcl/Tk that enables Vis5D to
    be used as an animation production system.  It also allows
    users to save and restore the full Vis5D state.  Vis5D
    can interpret a subset of Tcl internally, so installing
    Tcl is optional in order to use the scripting language.

  A new utility program, named v5dimport, that enables users
    to convert file formats, merge files, select data by location,
    time and field, resample data, and compress data.

  Iso-surfaces and motion trajectory ribbons can be colored
    according to the values of any scalar field.

  Wind streamlines.

  Interactive selection of any three fields for generating
    "wind" vectors, streamlines and trajectories.

  Pressure vertical coordinate system.

  Fields may occupy any interval of vertical levels (useful for
    merging atmosphere, ocean and surface data).

  Physical units can be specified for each field.

Version 4.2 is freely available.  It runs on Unix workstations
from SGI, IBM, HP, DEC and SUN, and also runs on PC's under Linux.

To get Vis5D, see the Web page at:

  http://www.ssec.wisc.edu/~billh/vis5d.html

