Hi,

We are having a big problem, which we cannot solve:

1. terminal server ----->  VMS  +  UCX ------> PPP server
2. terminal server --------------------------> PPP server


According to combination nu. 1 we create telnet on VMS  system,
which uses UCX, and from that point onwards  rlogin  /eight  on
PPP server. According to combination nu.  2  we  create  telnet
only on PPP server. PPP connection is always restored correctly
and operates without any problem. When  testing  the  lines  in
both cases we used for FTP transfer a  database  including  all
ASCII characters from 0 to 225; the upload and download of  the
database worked correctly. The only problem  we  have  now  and
which we cannot solve is a combination of  254  characters  and
one more character following  the  last  one,  which  can't  be
defined and I don't know it, unfortunately. At this  point  the
FTP connection to the database is interrupted and the upload is
not possible while the download works  normally.  This  problem
arises only at combination nu. 1, when we try to access the PPP
server through VMS. Combination nu. 2 works  correctly  on  the
other hand. Although we used VMS version 5.5-2  and  6.2  while
UCX version was 3.2, 3.3 and 4.0, we always  hit  on  the  same
problem:  a  combination  of  0xFE  characters  and  one   more
character following it disturbs  the process and FTP connection
is interrupted. Telnet, on the other hand, works on without any
problem through the same connection.

I wonder if anybody can suggest us how to adjust  UCX,  telnetd
and rlogin, and if it is  possible  in  VMS  at  all,  for  the
process working correctly.  For  the  time  beeing  a  solution
without VMS is not useable. Terminal has been set to:

set term/pasthru/passall/eight.


I also discover, that is zmodem (process) interrupted when I send problematic file. 

Here is message which I was found today:

%SYSTEM-W-DEVOFFLINE, device is not in configuration or not available
%RLOGIN-E-INTERNAL, Internal error
]}IK|)Y/-CdR#d4SGJHpW_buffer space available to reissue the AST

On the client side (I send file from WIN95 with Hyper terminal) I receive the message:

transfer interrupted on client request. 

Only data connection is broken, I can continue with my work normaly (dir, set def
etc.).
When I change the speed on modem (from 28800bps to 4800 bps), I could upload the file. 

With FTP sessions I have the same problem - DATA connection is broken, CONTROL
connection stay (I can browse on the directories normaly).

Thank you very much in advance.

Regards,   Milan

