organization: Atria Software, Inc.
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.sys.dec

My experience with Digital UNIX cross-version compatibility has been
quite pleasant.

DEC OSF/1 V2.0 binaries (shared linkage) still run fine on DUNIX T4.0-2
(2nd beta test), and I expect no problems with the final DUNIX V4.0.
V3.2 shared binaries run fine as well.  I don't have specific experience
with statically linked programs, but I would not expect any problems.

If there are DEC OSF/1 features you use which have been retired as of
DUNIX V4.0, you might have problems, but I wouldn't expect any problems
otherwise.

