In article <wn20lnfbsi.fsf@heidi.came.sbg.ac.at>,
Peter Lackner <plo@Heidi.came.sbg.ac.at> wrote:
>Hi all,
>
>I'd like to use an EXABYTE 8505XL drive on a DEC 3000/400 (OSF1 V2.0). 
>Anybody out there who uses this configuration? 
>What do I  have to do to make it run?
>

Sure we use a lot of EXEBYTE 8505s.  Simply attach the device
to the scsi bus, reboot machine and run the appropriate 
MAKEDEV command.

For example, 1) bring down system
             2) attach device
   	     3) bring system up
             4) cd /dev;
             5) ./MAKEDEV tz## 
               
That's it.  MAKEDEV will make the /dev/(n)rmt0? files.

Steve Mc



