Hi Alex,

  
In message <829695560.26001@sushi.demon.co.uk>,  said:

  > I have just been given a hard disk drive its about 18" long 12" wide
  > and about 9" deep it looks like a land mine!!! could anyone give me
  > help what is it it has a scsi connection block and a model no. kb
  > r82 should i call the bomb squad or get it running
  
   This sounds like it may be an RA82 HDA (HDA = Hard Disk Assembly).
  The model number 'kb' concurs with a kb##### serial number,
  'kb' being the manufacturing code for Kaufbeuren in Germany,
  where they were made.
   Does it have 'fins' running along the top side, from front to
  back, and four holes on lugs at each corner; is there a circular
  hub on the underside, and a lever on the top side near the
  front which says 'lock'/'unlock'. If so, it definitely sounds like
  an RA82 HDA.
   If there is an electronic module on the top with a berg connector
  on the rear and at the front, with the one at the front being
  connected via. a grey flat cable to another board on the front
  face, this is not a SCSI board but the Read/Module which was
  connected to the rest of the RA82 disk drive via. a flat cable
  on the rear berg connector.
  
   Hope this helps, perhaps there is no need to call the bomb squad :-)
   

   Best Regards,
   Brian
   
   brobson@cix.compulink.co.uk
   
    




