 2 instruction for 64bit... you could design the cpu to execute 2
 instruction in 1 cycle with little effort by having a rule where no
 destination can overlap. So its the compiler job, not the CPU to make 
 sure this is true. the CPU cannot stall on register conflict because all
 operation are fully concurent.

 Or you can see it as a dual CPU sharing a registerfile and cache but for 
