>Don't know how they can improve memory performance, since I am not Digital's
>Engineer.:-) But they have to do so since HP can do so. The current design of
>alpha's memory subsystem just can not catch up its super fast CPU. Do you have  any idea about the on-board cache and main memory latency of a typical alpha
>box? I can not remember exactly but they are much slower than CPU. If your
>program can not fit into its on-chip cache, you are out of luck, your program
>may slow down ten times. If you like to work on a dumb text terminal a 9MB VAX
>may be ok for you. BUt it just can not work for current applications.
>I think they can not go for 100% static since it is too expensive. Even 100%
>static is still not enough since the static cache is still very slow compare
>to a 400MHz or 500MHz CPU.
