>I cannot read or write files in native Office 4.2 or 4.3 format to or
>from the network drive.  By this I mean in Word 6.0 or Excel 5.0
>format.  

One guess:
Turn off the ultrix locking on the file server. Here a snippet from the 
release notes:


        Locking and Sharing Violations

        Problem: Some recent versions of PC applications experience
        locking problems with PATHWORKS when UltrixLockingEnabled is
        set to "yes". For example, Microsoft Word version 6.0 (can
        not save *.doc files), Excel version 5.0 (can not read/write
        spreadsheet files), and Paradox (problems with Engine).

        Solution: The reason for this problem is that the application
        is setting a lock at a very high offset in a file to provide
        semaphore-like operations for itself. The offset is legal
        to DOS but exceeds the Ultrix limit. The solution for this
        problem is to set "UltrixLockingEnabled" to NO in the lanman.ini
        file. The PATHWORKS server contains a private lock manager
        which is able to satisfy all lock requests which is always
        enabled.

Esa Laitinen
Digital Equipment Corporation Oy




