Ahh, But I might point out that the HP PA-8000 beats the Alpha 400 MHz now.
              SpecInt95    SpecFP95
     PA-8000    11.8         20.2     (And all at only 180 MHz)
     A21164     11.0         14.0     (As Quoted from DEC for the 400 MHz alpha)

I think that a trend starts to become apparent, in that DEC tends to handly performance, not by 
optimizing, but rather by blugeoning the chip with speed. Where as other chip makers have spent 
some time to optimize, and use more "elegant" solutions. I also think it's humorous to note 
that the reason DEC felt the need to push the alpha to 400 and 500 so soon, was because the 
Pentium Pro was impinging on their low end (The PentPro 200 is faster than the high end 21064, 
