into the conversation, and a barrage of comments on how "they" will never make a chip as fast 
or as cool as blah company's chip, I would like to point out that Intel and HP co-developed the 
HP PA-8000, and that, I wouldn't doubt that when the P7 finally does come out, It will borrow 
heavily on this instruction set and design (Come on when have you known Intel to give something 
without taking their fair share) making one fast chip for the masses.






