In article <4kd7ue$3jo@news00.btx.dtag.de>, 053176195-0001@t-online.de (Klaus Schwarze) writes:
|>I tried to connect a NEC D3817 SCSI harddisk to a VS 3100 M76. That drive 
|>is recognized during boot (show device works), but I cannot access it 
|>from VMS (V5.5). All I get is a "fatal drive error".
|>
|>Any help would be appreciated.
|>
|>Klaus Schwarze

I'm not sure it's causing your problem, but we had a problem
putting a new disk drive on a 3100/76. The VAXstation 3100/76 is a
SCSI1 device. If the drive is a SCSI2 drive, which is almost a certainty 
unless it's really old, the 3100 running VMS 5.5 can not deal with it. 

SCSI2 devices send more information than SCSI1 when communicating, 
VMS 5.5 sees it as overflow, and the drive is marked as offline. Ours
continuously dismounted and mounted. I believe there's a patch
for VMS 5.5-2, but don't know if it goes all the way down to 
VMS 5.5. They included the patch in VMS 6.2.

We hadn't upgraded at that point, and weren't ready to. We 
returned the new disk (ours was a Seagate) and got a DEC drive
instead, which worked because all DEC equipment is compatible. ;-)
 
