> I read this morning where the Windows NT work was being moved from DEC's
> SPU (Alpha) to the PCBU (Intel). Does anyone know the real impact of this?

The impact will be to simplify "one-stop shopping" for WNT solutions.
Instead of going to both the SBU and PCBU for an Intel-based WNT solution,
everything will now be handled by the PCBU.

> Is Alpha "being dumped" from NT corporately?

No way Jose. WNT is crucial to Alpha volumes. The Alpha XL Dream Machines
are selling quite well, and WNT now goes out on perhaps ~25 percent of
AlphaServers. Over time, (if the strategy works) WNT will be the engine
that drives low-end Alpha sales.

> 
