Re: Help with Decstation 3100

I can help you with the power-up messages of your VS. I copied some of 
the DEC information for you:

Every time you turn the system on, the system runs power-up tests. These 
tests check each device installed in your system. As each device is 
tested, a test number is diplayed on the screen. If the sequence 
displayed during power-up contains question marks or asterisks, failures 
may exist in the system.

Table: Device identifiers in power-up and self-tests

F    -    Base video
E    -    System clock
D    -    Nonvolatile RAM
C    -    Serial line controller
B    -    Memory
A    -    Memory management unit
9    -    Floating point unit
8    -    Interval timer
7    -    SCSI-A bus controller
6    -    SCSI-B bus controller
5    -    Interrupt controller and Ethernet ID rom
4    -    Graphics coporocessor
3    - 
2    -  
1    -    Ethernet network interconnect

It looks like you have a problem with your network connection. If you get
the message  ?? 1  00C0  0000.7004 that may indicate
o No cable on ThinWire (BNC) Ethernet connectors
o No terminator on the ThinWire port
o Network select button in the wrong position (in=ThinWire out=AUI)
o Faulty cable or loose connection

If you get the message ?? 1 00C0 0011.700E that may indicate
o No cable on the standard (AUI) connector.
o No loopbach connector at the AUI port.
o Network select button in the wrong position.
o Faulty cable.

My advice is to connect a T-connector with 2 50Ohms terminators to the 
BNC connector and the loopback connector (15pin with a LED) to the AUI 
connector. If the error is still persistent you might have a problem with 
your Ethernet hardware. If the system is OK after this, you can connect 
it to your local network. Make sure that the network select button 
(located between the ThinWire BNC connector and the 15-pin Sub-D AUI 
connector) is set to the right position.

If you don�t want to connect to a network you need not worry about that 
error message.

To find out the storage capacity of your disk drives, enter "show device" 
in console mode.

Klaus Schwarze 




