It should work fine with the PC keyboard. Have you set the keyboard type in 
Session Manager? I'm not aware of any LK450 drivers for Windows NT.

> Is there any graphics board other than the Qvision 1024 which will work
> with both VMS and NT? Will the Qvision 1280 work with both?

Stick with the Qvision you have. The SOC lists supported hardware options.

> It appears that the memory consists of standard 72 pin 70ns parity SIMMs.
> Is this true?  What sizes can be used? I assume that they have to be
> replaced in sets of 4, correct?

From the Technical Manual (dated Feb 1993):

The system unit supports eight memory module connectors on the system module. 
These memory connectors are logically grouped in two memory banks. Each memory 
option supported by the system consists of four memory modules. When you install 
a memory option in a memory bank, you must install a memory module in all of the 
connectors in that bank.

Supported memory options are PB20M-DB 16MB and PB20M-FC 64MB.
