> 2x42bit organisation? Or it is a simple 36bit module?
> Any hints? What does it means ECC? Is there any error
> correction/detection, or it is a simple parity check there?

The Alpha based Multia is based on the DECchip 21066 Alpha chip.
It has a built-in ECC (2 bit detection, single bit correction) memory
controller.

The SIMMs in the Multia are standard PC style 36 bit SIMMs.

