> Well, if you looked closely to the block diagram
> of the ICU, it only dispatches 4 instruction per
> cycle (ref. IBM J. Res. Develop, vol38, no.5, pp.
> 504 figure one).  
> 
> Same as the PPC series.
> 
> However if there're 6 instruction in the reservation 
> stations, it can issue 6.

No. No. No.  Take another look at the figure and then carefully reread
Krste's list.  While the ICU (which contains the I-cache, the branch
and CR logical units and instruction dispatch) appears to dispatch only
4 inst/cycle to the FXU & FPU chips, the branch & CR logical units on
the ICU chip can also tap off up to 2 additional inst/cycle from the
dispatch unit in parallel with the 4 inst/cycle dispatch to the integer
& FP units for a total of 6 inst/cycle.

