Chris Scheers wrote:
> It appears that the memory consists of standard 72 pin 70ns parity SIMMs.
> Is this true?  What sizes can be used? I assume that they have to be
> replaced in sets of 4, correct?

	Yep.  Be _very_ carefull about the memory you replace it with.  It
HAS to be 70ns parity, no slower, no faster.  I got three shipments of 60ns
memory for one of our AXPs and none of the shipments worked.  I _believe_
you can use any density SIMM, but I'm not sure.

	They do have to be done in 4s, and you have to remember to stagger
them on the motherboard.  One slot is bank 0, then the next is bank 1, then
the next is bank 0, etc.

						Jason
