The latest figures I heard for testing on the PA-8000 (prerelease, obviously)
pegged the numbers at 11.something SPEC95int, 20.2 SPEC95fp.  HP will begin
shipping their K-class line with PA-8000 CPUs sometime this month.  They might
squeeze a couple more tenths out of those numbers by the time the official
numbers are released.  Given that DEC's highest SPECint is also 11.something,
I have to wonder if HP isn't dragging their feet on the official announcement
of the machines until they can tune their compilers enough to edge out the
