sondak@galileo.res.utc.com (Doug Sondak	) wrote:

DEC Fortran 77 has an option on the OPEN statement called 
"CONVERT" that allows you to change the input/output of data files
that you work with. This are options  little-endiad, big-endiad,
vax-d, vax-g, etc. The Fortran run time will convert them on the fly.
If you standardize on big-endiad (RS6000 format ?)  for your
unformatted data files you should be OK. You could not easily write a
program to convert the files  to RS6000 format unless you knew every
variable type that was being written out and its offset in the file.

>Although I am using an IBM workstation, I work closely with a
