Marv Penner <pennerm@siast.sk.ca> wrote:

>I am having trouble getting the exact pin outs for attaching a US 
>Robotics 28.8 modem to a Decserver 90M via RS232C.  I need to build a 
>patch from an 8 pin RJ45 jack from the server to a 25 pin RS232C.  Does 
>anyone have some ideas on this ????

What you need is a DEC H8585-AC:

RJ-45 	                DB-25 (M)
1 Blue                        7
2 Orange  	       3
3 Black                     (7)
4 Red      	       5
5 Green   	       4
6 Yellow  	       2
7 Brown                    20
8 White                     6

Notice  pins 1 and 3 are tied to the pin 7 on the DB-25.


Calvin Chung




